From 4ff516439fe28fdfbf09e30aed516e7e943e585a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:58:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(circadian): allow a live date with a fixed location
 (DB-084)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The store and CircadianWindowProvider have always resolved the fixed date
and the fixed location independently, but the Circadian card could only
express two of the three combinations: its Set button took a non-null
String date and refused a blank one, so pinning coordinates always pinned
that day's date as well. The cause is the control's shape — the coordinate
fields treat blank as "live", while the date is a button that always
renders a day, so "live" had no representation and the rendered day was
read as the user's choice. Tasker's picker simply left %AAB_Date empty,
which is how the owner noticed.

Live-vs-fixed now has its own dateFixed flag and a "Live date" button, and
the status line gains the third reading it was already shaped for. No
change to the store, the provider or the pipeline.

Verified: scripts/ladder.sh green (build + JVM/Robolectric tests + guards).
New unit tests cover location-only at the card and at the provider, and the
date-only card test now pins its date through the picker. Not checkable
locally: on-device behaviour — the owner's step is DEVICE_TEST_SCRIPT §7
21a, queued in STATE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
